OL,3,ANew York court hears arguments in
OL,4,Aongoing 9/11 families' lawsuit against
OL,5,ASaudi Arabia
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe Court of Appeals in New York has
OL,8,Fheard arguments from both lawyers for
OL,9,Ffamilies of 9/11 victims and the
OL,10,Fgovernment of Saudi Arabia as it
OL,11,Fdecides whether the families'
OL,12,Flong-running legal case against the
OL,13,FMiddle Eastern country can move to
OL,14,Ftrial.
OL,16,FAlmost 3,000 people were killed on 11
OL,17,FSeptember 2001 after hijackers seized
OL,18,Ffour US passenger jets and crashed them
OL,19,Finto the World Trade Center in New
OL,20,FYork, the Pentagon, and a Pennsylvania
OL,21,Ffield, following resistance from
OL,22,Fpassengers.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,317,300,200,140,0,100
