OL,2,W//%*// //%Q%**,$-.,%,. (,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ANew York court hears arguments in
OL,4,Aongoing 9/11 families' lawsuit against
OL,5,ASaudi Arabia
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe families allege that a Saudi
OL,8,Fgovernment employee, Omar al-Bayoumi,
OL,9,Fknowingly supported two of the
OL,10,Fhijackers and that he was working with
OL,11,Fa network of officials linked to the
OL,12,FSaudi Ministry of Islamic Affairs.
OL,14,FBayoumi, who is now retired from
OL,15,Fgovernment work, has denied knowing the
OL,16,Ftwo men were hijackers or that he had
OL,17,Fany involvement in 9/11, while Saudi
OL,18,FArabia has said that any allegation
OL,19,Fthat it or its officials are complicit
OL,20,Fin 9/11 is categorically false.
OL,23,APub: 07-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
